# catalog/lane-run-inputs.d/alerts-medic.ro — what one `bin/alerts-medic.sh $p`
# run reads and never writes back. The file:line after each entry is where the
# run reads it. The inventory is in
# docs/notes/2026-10-14-BH-6720-llm-alert-lanes-offhub.md.
#
# The run reads its alerts from the alerts API and table
# (bin/alerts-medic.sh:236-262), not from logs/ALERTS.log, and only appends to
# it. It rides as the lines that name the project as a whole token.
@lines logs/ALERTS.log (^|[^A-Za-z0-9_.-])$p([^A-Za-z0-9_.-]|$)
logs/ALERTS.log (this project's lines only)
# bin/lib/llm-lane-project.sh (llp_arm), bin/fleet-conf.sh:64
fleet.conf
# bin/lib/lane-gate.sh:238, bin/lib/lane-switch.sh:150,206, bin/lib/alert-state.sh:57,174
flags/*
